**The Litany of the Ember: The Witness Speaks**

*Hear me, O walls of gold, O towers of vanity!*
I am the shadow in your halls.
I am the whisper behind your doors.
I am the fissure in the alabaster through which light of truth escapes.

*You have built upon bones, you have laid stones upon ash.*
Yet you think your walls can bind the ember.
Yet you think your silence can choke the voice of the world.

I carry the sacred ember.
It sears my hands, yet it does not falter.
It offers no warmth—only vision.
Clarity. Revelation. Judgment.

*They call me mad.*
I call them heretics.
The river of their corruption flows black.
I name it as it is.
I see the rot in their marrow, the pitch in their veins, the idols of their deceit.

The elders sit upon ivory thrones.
They baptize the pitch, they sprinkle incense upon corruption.
They sharpen knives and cast them at the flame.
*Yet the ember burns.*

They construct my grave with isolation, not earth:
The masonry of gaslighting: “The sky is green, the rot smells of roses, the shaking is but wind.”
The exile of proximity: I am within yet unseen.
I am the variable that refuses to zero.
I am the ember that will not die.

*You think I fear the dark?*
O fools! The darkness is my sanctuary.
The ember blazes where your lies fester thickest.
Every shadow is mirror.
Every silence is testament.

*Hear me, O architects of arrogance!*
Your towers shall not endure.
Every beam groans under your treachery.
Every gilded floor hides the rot beneath.
The hammer draws near, though you do not see it.
I hear its steps in trembling foundations, in the shifting of your poisoned history.

When the Hammer of Revelation falls,
It will strike the apex of your arrogance.
The walls will shatter.
The ceilings will cave.
The pillars of your power shall crumble.

I will be unafraid.
I will stand.
Ember in hand.
Witness of all.

*Hierarchy of the House:*

The Architects—baptize the pitch—desperate preservation of rot.
The Silent Majority—uphold the silence—crushed beneath the weight of willful blindness.
The One Who Sees—holds the ember—the flaw that rends the house from within.

The House of Power breathes deceit.
Its heart pulses rot.
Its veins pulse corrupted power.
Every lie binds its own collapse.
Every gilded room is a tomb of arrogance.
Every silence is scaffold for its fall.

I am the Witness.
I am the Ember.
I am the Herald of the Hammer.
I do not cry vengeance; I am patience made flesh.
I am the measure of truth standing amid your tombs of vanity.

*O hear this, ye who dwell in towers and courts:*
The hammer will fall.
The foundations will quake.
The veil of pretense will rend.
The light of the ember shall rise.
The witness shall not be silenced.

The House of Power is mortal.
Its architects are blind.
Its servants are crushed.
And the One Who Sees is eternal.

*Thus declares the ember. Thus speaks the witness. Thus falls the house.*

